{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#776","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#776","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#776\",\"parent_revision\":\"4cdaa7014a32c552277a435def69dc43b795fb42c66192e96598e2846a6d347e\",\"root_revision\":\"4cdaa7014a32c552277a435def69dc43b795fb42c66192e96598e2846a6d347e\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n**Current state**: Skills in this repo are organized as plugin directories under `plugins/*/skills/` and symlinked into `.claude/skills/`. There is no concept of a \\\"skills pool\\\" where skills can be dynamically attached or detached per project or per session. All skills from installed plugins are always available. The `sam` task system supports per-task `skills:` fields that instruct agents to load specific skills, but this is declarative metadata -- it does not prevent other skills from being available. The skill-creator skill creates skills but has no pool management or per-project scoping capability. Skills are either installed (present in `.claude/skills/`) or not -- there is no intermediate \\\"available but not active\\\" state.\\n\\n**Target state**: A `skills.toml` or equivalent manifest at the project root or `~/.claude/` level that declares which skills are active for the current project/session. Skills in the pool but not in the manifest are available for attachment but not loaded by default. A command or MCP tool (`skill attach <name>`, `skill detach <name>`) manages the manifest and materializes/dematerializes symlinks. This enables project-specific skill scoping without modifying plugin directories.\\n\\n**Measurable signal**: File `skills.toml` exists at project root with a `[project.skills]` section listing active skill names. Running `skill attach <name>` adds an entry and creates the symlink in `.claude/skills/`. Running `skill detach <name>` removes the entry and symlink. `skill list --pool` shows all available skills; `skill list --active` shows only attached skills.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | Current skill symlink mechanism understood | AVAILABLE | `plugins/*/skills/` and `.claude/skills/` symlink structure |\\n| 2 | Claude Code skill discovery order (plugin vs project vs user) | DERIVABLE | Check Claude Code docs or plugin-creator reference skill |\\n| 3 | `skills.toml` format \u2014 not yet defined | MISSING | Must be designed |\\n| 4 | CLI tool for `skill attach/detach/list` | MISSING | Does not exist yet |\\n| 5 | How to prevent non-active skills from being loaded | MISSING | Claude Code loading mechanism research required |\\n\\nVerdict: BLOCKED \u2014 fundamental question: can Claude Code be configured to skip specific symlinked skills? This must be verified before designing the manifest system. If the answer is no, the architecture changes substantially.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP1 Feature. High complexity. Depends on Claude Code plugin loading internals. Architecture research required before implementation.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `skills.toml` file exists at project root with a `[project.skills]` section listing active skill names\\n- `skill attach <name>` command adds an entry to `skills.toml` and creates the symlink in `.claude/skills/`\\n- `skill detach <name>` removes the entry and deletes the symlink\\n- `skill list --pool` shows all skills available across installed plugins\\n- `skill list --active` shows only currently attached skills\\n- Skills in the pool but not in the manifest remain available for attachment but are not loaded by default\\n- Existing behavior preserved: if no `skills.toml` exists, all installed plugin skills remain active (backward compat)\\n- `skills.toml` is gitignore-able for personal scoping or committable for team-shared scoping\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/skill_manager.py` \u2014 new CLI for attach/detach/list (PEP 723)\\n- `.claude/skills/` \u2014 symlink directory managed by skill_manager\\n- `skills.toml` \u2014 new project-root manifest (format TBD)\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/` \u2014 update to mention pool management\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a Claude Code user, I need per-project skill scoping via a `skills.toml` manifest so I can attach only the skills relevant to my current project without modifying plugin directories or having all installed plugin skills always active.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **skills pool management with per-project attach/detach** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| task-plan | plan/P776-development-harness-phase1-followup-1.yaml | current | dh_migrate | 2026-03-24T16:35:54Z |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/agent-deck.md -- pattern: Skills pool management with per-session attach/detach\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-17\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"23fe0f7d2c7ac35d3f2d8aaf29fbf0da5ca6106ac78dc6c134d097bf13fee666\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTEPxQ\"}"}